import{c as t,Q as o,j as i,m as n}from"./chunks/framework.BXc4yaFE.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Loop-Driven Development: The Next Layer of AI Coding","description":"","frontmatter":{"url":"https://x.com/bibryam/status/2065445933601435823","title":"Loop-Driven Development: The Next Layer of AI Coding","author":"Bilgin Ibryam","archived":"2026-06-13T00:00:00.000Z","domains":["ai-coding","agentic-workflows","developer-tooling"],"external_link":"https://generativeprogrammer.com/p/from-test-driven-to-loop-driven-development","followers":83042,"handle":"bibryam","platform":"twitter","published":"2026-06-12T00:00:00.000Z","ratings":{"signal":5,"novelty":4,"actionability":4,"durability":4,"relevance":5,"total":22},"stats":{"likes":228,"retweets":44,"replies":4,"views":15348},"tags":["loop-engineering","harness-engineering","context-engineering","tdd","verification","ai-agents"],"type":"article"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"research/tweets/2026-06-12-@bibryam-435823.md","filePath":"research/tweets/2026-06-12-@bibryam-435823.md","lastUpdated":1785909234000}'),a={name:"research/tweets/2026-06-12-@bibryam-435823.md"};function r(s,e,l,d,h,p){return o(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n(`<h2 id="中文摘要" tabindex="-1">中文摘要 <a class="header-anchor" href="#中文摘要" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;中文摘要&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Bilgin Ibryam（Red Hat 出身、《Kubernetes Patterns》作者）將 AI coding 的演進歸納為<strong>五個階段</strong>，每階段都在拓寬「迴圈內的工作單元」：</p><ol><li><strong>Autocomplete Era</strong>（自動補全）— 模型補下一個編輯（Copilot/Cursor Tab）。加入：model + 本地檔案 context + inline completion。好處=速度，限制=範疇（不擁有任務）。</li><li><strong>Prompt Engineering Era</strong>（提示工程）— 從補全進化到任務操控。加入：goal + instructions + tools + prompt loop。好處=委派，限制=收斂（無清楚停止條件會漂移）。</li><li><strong>Context Engineering Era</strong>（情境工程）— 瓶頸變成 agent 能看到什麼。加入：repo context + terminal + 檔案編輯 + 測試執行。好處=範疇，限制=正確性（環境無法定義「done」仍會做錯事）。</li><li><strong>Harness Engineering Era</strong>（框架工程）— harness = 單次 agent run 周邊環境（prompts/tools/sandbox/permissions/tests/CI/evals/review gates）。加入：sandbox + verifier + permissions + CI/eval harness + review boundaries。好處=可重複性，限制=連續性（單次 run 變安全，但真實工作跨失敗/事件/審查/排程延續）。</li><li><strong>Loop Engineering Era</strong>（迴圈工程）— 下一層。Loop ≠ automation：automation 執行固定步驟；loop 檢查結果、決定是否繼續、用回饋改進下一輪。工程師不再只寫 code/prompt，而是<strong>設計讓 agent 能安全持續工作的系統</strong>。</li></ol><p><strong>核心論點</strong>：從 TDD → LDD（Loop-Driven Development）。舊迴圈 = 寫測試→通過→重構；新迴圈 = <strong>設定意圖 → 跑 agent → 驗證結果 → 修復失敗 → 重複或升級</strong>。關鍵詞不是「AI」而是 <strong>verify</strong>——沒有驗證就只是「重複提示」（repeated prompting），不是 loop；有驗證 loop 才能收斂。</p><h2 id="與-workspace-的關聯" tabindex="-1">與 workspace 的關聯 <a class="header-anchor" href="#與-workspace-的關聯" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;與 workspace 的關聯&quot;">​</a></h2><p>直接呼應 cc-workspace 的 <strong>The Loop</strong> 行為契約（OBSERVE→IDENTIFY→PROPOSE→APPLY→TEST→RECORD 六階段元迴圈）：</p><ul><li>作者的「verify 是 loop 的本質」= core.md TEST 階段的 <strong>unverified_success 閘門</strong>（subagent 自報成功 = 中間態，主對話親跑確定性檢查才升 verified）。</li><li>「set intent → run agent → verify → repair → repeat or escalate」≈ workspace 的 IDENTIFY（成功條件）→ APPLY → TEST → 失敗 ≥3 次委派 self-escalate 收斂判斷。</li><li>Harness Engineering Era 的 verifier/eval/review gates = workspace 的 healthcheck.sh / deep-review / APPLY 前置 gate。</li><li>本文可作為 workspace「為何強制 The Loop 而非單純 prompt」的外部理論背書。</li></ul><h2 id="評分-5-維-各-5-分-總-25" tabindex="-1">評分（5 維 / 各 5 分，總 25） <a class="header-anchor" href="#評分-5-維-各-5-分-總-25" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;評分（5 維 / 各 5 分，總 25）&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>維度</th><th>分數</th><th>理由</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Signal（訊號密度）</td><td>5</td><td>五階段分類乾淨，每階段「加入什麼/好處/限制」結構一致，無灌水</td></tr><tr><td>Novelty（新穎度）</td><td>4</td><td>「五階段」框架是既有概念的清晰整合（非全新），但 LDD 命名與 verify-centric 論點有辨識度</td></tr><tr><td>Actionability（可操作性）</td><td>4</td><td>給出明確的新迴圈公式（set intent→verify→repair→escalate），可直接對映到 agent 系統設計</td></tr><tr><td>Durability（持久性）</td><td>4</td><td>階段論可能隨工具演進再加層，但 verify-as-convergence 的核心洞見穩定</td></tr><tr><td>Relevance（相關性）</td><td>5</td><td>與 workspace The Loop 契約幾乎一對一映射，極高</td></tr><tr><td><strong>總分</strong></td><td><strong>22/25</strong></td><td>高價值，建議納入 harness 理論引用</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2 id="原文全文-英文" tabindex="-1">原文全文（英文） <a class="header-anchor" href="#原文全文-英文" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;原文全文（英文）&quot;">​</a></h2><h2 id="coding-has-always-been-in-loops-write-code-run-it-check-the-result-change-it-repeat-that-loop-is-older-than-ai-tdd-made-it-explicit-with-red-green-refactor-bdd-widened-it-toward-behaviour-acceptance-testing-widened-it-toward-user-intent-ci-widened-it-toward-delivery-so-when-people-talk-about-loop-engineering-the-interesting-question-is-not-whether-software-has-loops-it-always-did-the-question-is-what-is-inside-the-loop-now-with-ai-coding-the-unit-of-work-keeps-getting-wider-it-used-to-be-a-line-a-function-or-a-failing-test-now-it-can-be-a-task-a-pull-request-a-migration-or-a-recurring-workflow-i-think-ai-coding-has-moved-rapidly-through-five-phases" tabindex="-1">Coding has always been in loops. Write code, run it, check the result, change it, repeat. That loop is older than AI. TDD made it explicit with red, green, refactor. BDD widened it toward behaviour. Acceptance testing widened it toward user intent. CI widened it toward delivery. So when people talk about loop engineering, the interesting question is not whether software has loops. It always did. The question is: what is inside the loop now? With AI coding, the unit of work keeps getting wider. It used to be a line, a function, or a failing test. Now it can be a task, a pull request, a migration, or a recurring workflow. I think AI coding has moved rapidly through five phases. <a class="header-anchor" href="#coding-has-always-been-in-loops-write-code-run-it-check-the-result-change-it-repeat-that-loop-is-older-than-ai-tdd-made-it-explicit-with-red-green-refactor-bdd-widened-it-toward-behaviour-acceptance-testing-widened-it-toward-user-intent-ci-widened-it-toward-delivery-so-when-people-talk-about-loop-engineering-the-interesting-question-is-not-whether-software-has-loops-it-always-did-the-question-is-what-is-inside-the-loop-now-with-ai-coding-the-unit-of-work-keeps-getting-wider-it-used-to-be-a-line-a-function-or-a-failing-test-now-it-can-be-a-task-a-pull-request-a-migration-or-a-recurring-workflow-i-think-ai-coding-has-moved-rapidly-through-five-phases" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Coding has always been in loops.
Write code, run it, check the result, change it, repeat. That loop is older than AI. TDD made it explicit with red, green, refactor. BDD widened it toward behaviour. Acceptance testing widened it toward user intent. CI widened it toward delivery.
So when people talk about loop engineering, the interesting question is not whether software has loops. It always did.
The question is: what is inside the loop now?
With AI coding, the unit of work keeps getting wider. It used to be a line, a function, or a failing test. Now it can be a task, a pull request, a migration, or a recurring workflow.
I think AI coding has moved rapidly through five phases.&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Autocomplete Era The model helped with the next edit. Copilot and Cursor Tab made this mainstream. The loop was still mostly human-controlled: type, inspect, accept or reject, continue. What got added: → model → local file context → inline completion The benefit was speed. The limit was scope. The model helped write the next piece of code, but it did not own the task.</li></ol><hr><ol start="2"><li>Prompt Engineering Era The model moved from completion to task steering. You could ask for a script, a test suite, an explanation, or a migration plan. The loop became: ask, generate, inspect, retry. What got added: → goal → instructions → tools → prompt loop The benefit was delegation. The limit was convergence. A prompt loop without good context or a clear stop condition can drift, repeat itself, or finish the wrong thing.</li></ol><hr><ol start="3"><li>Context Engineering Era Once agents could act, the bottleneck became what they could see. A coding agent needs more than a prompt. It needs files, tests, logs, conventions, architecture notes, issue history, and current repo state. The loop became repo-aware: read context, edit files, run commands, inspect result. What got added: → repo context → terminal access → file editing → test execution The benefit was scope. The limit was correctness. A well-contextualized agent can still do the wrong thing if the environment cannot tell it what done means.</li></ol><hr><ol start="4"><li>Harness Engineering Era A harness is the environment around one agent run. It includes prompts, tools, repo context, sandbox, permissions, tests, linters, type checks, CI, evals, and review gates. The loop became constrained and checkable. What got added: → sandbox → verifier →permissions →CI and eval harness → review boundaries The benefit was repeatability. The limit was continuity. One agent run can be made safer, but real work often continues across failures, events, reviews, schedules, and state.</li></ol><hr><ol start="5"><li>Loop Engineering Era This is the next layer. A loop is not just automation. Automation executes fixed steps. A loop checks the result, decides whether to continue, and uses feedback to improve the next iteration. That is where AI coding starts to look different. The engineer is no longer only writing code or prompts. The engineer is designing the system that lets an agent keep working safely. The shift looks like this: → Autocomplete made coding faster. → Prompting made generation broader. → Context made agents repo-aware. → Harnesses made agent runs checkable. → Loops make agent work repeatable. That is the move from test-driven development to loop-driven development. Not because tests stop mattering. Because tests become one part of a larger loop. The old loop was: write test, make it pass, refactor. The new loop is: set intent, run agent, verify result, repair failure, repeat or escalate. The important word is not “AI.” The important word is verify. Without verification, you do not have a loop. You have repeated prompting. With verification, the loop can converge. Software engineering was always a loop. AI is widening the loop again.</li></ol><hr><p>Build the loop. Stay the engineer. 👉 I wrote the full version with diagrams, examples, and the full evolution from autocomplete to loop engineering here: [圖 1 — 來源: The Evolution of AI-Assisted Coding Overview] <a href="https://generativeprogrammer.com/p/from-test-driven-to-loop-driven-development" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://generativeprogrammer.com/p/from-test-driven-to-loop-driven-development</a></p>`,23)])])}const u=t(a,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,u as default};
